{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall set bounds.</b> Set a boundary on the mountain, like it, \"set bounds to the mountain and sanctify it\" (below, Exodus 23 [?]). [Meaning:] to set a boundary on the mountain. And I have drawn this out at such length because the madman said in his book, turning the words of the living Elohim upside down, that Moses meant \"set bounds on the people,\" and \"the mountain\" came out of his mouth in place of \"the people.\"" "<b>Whoever touches the mountain.</b> With his body."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The citation 'למטה פ' כך' ('below, chapter 23') likely refers to Exodus 23, but the specific verse is uncertain; the quoted phrase does not appear verbatim in Exodus 23."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:53.502028239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}